#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:3
msgid "How pipx works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:7
msgid ""
"This page describes the **pip backend** model, where a shared `pip <https://"
"pip.pypa.io>`_ environment backs every managed venv through a ``.pth`` file. "
"When the **uv backend** is active (the default whenever `uv <https://"
"docs.astral.sh/uv/>`_ is available, via the ``pipx[uv]`` extra or on "
"``PATH``) pipx skips the shared environment and uses ``uv venv`` and ``uv "
"pip`` instead; uv-created venvs ship without ``pip``. See :doc:`../how-to/"
"use-uv-backend`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:15
msgid "Installing an application"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:17
msgid ""
"``pipx install PACKAGE`` creates an isolated virtual environment under "
"``PIPX_HOME`` (for example ``~/.local/share/pipx/venvs/black``) and installs "
"the package into it. Under the pip backend pipx creates the venv without "
"``pip``, then creates or reuses a shared environment that holds an up-to-"
"date ``pip`` and links it into the venv through a `.pth file <https://"
"docs.python.org/3/library/site.html>`_, so every venv borrows one ``pip`` "
"rather than installing its own. Under the uv backend there is no shared "
"environment: ``uv venv`` builds the venv (without ``pip``) and ``uv pip`` "
"installs into it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:24
msgid ""
"pipx refreshes the shared ``pip`` once it is more than 30 days old, or right "
"away when it is older than ``pip`` 26.2.2; ``pipx upgrade-shared`` refreshes "
"it immediately. When ``pip``'s files are missing from the shared "
"environment, pipx rebuilds it before running ``pip``. It also rebuilds "
"shared environments created with Python older than 3.10, which cannot "
"install the required ``pip`` version. Rebuilding uses the default Python "
"interpreter; existing applications' ``.pth`` references are refreshed before "
"their next installer operation. When a ``pip`` command fails because ``pip`` "
"no longer imports, pipx rebuilds it and retries the command once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:31
msgid ""
"After installing the package, pipx exposes the application's resources so "
"you can reach them from any directory. It handles three kinds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:34
msgid ""
"console and GUI scripts, into ``PIPX_BIN_DIR`` (default ``~/.local/bin``), "
"for example ``~/.local/bin/black`` -> ``~/.local/share/pipx/venvs/black/bin/"
"black``;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:36
msgid ""
"manual pages, into ``PIPX_MAN_DIR`` (default ``~/.local/share/man/"
"man[1-9]``);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:37
msgid ""
"shell completion scripts, into ``PIPX_COMPLETION_DIR`` (default ``~/.local/"
"share``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:39
msgid ""
"pipx symlinks each resource into place. On Windows it copies the file "
"instead when the target directory does not support symlinks. As long as "
"``PIPX_BIN_DIR`` is on your ``PATH`` the commands are available globally, "
"and on systems with ``man`` support the pages are too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:43
msgid ""
"pipx records what it installed and exposed in a per-venv "
"``pipx_metadata.json`` file. Later commands (``upgrade``, ``reinstall``, "
"``expose``) read it to reproduce the same state. When an upgrade or "
"reinstall changes the resources a package ships, pipx exposes the new ones "
"and deletes the links or copies of the ones the package dropped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:47
msgid ""
"Adding ``--global`` to any command targets a system-wide location shared by "
"all users instead of your home directory; the concrete paths and overrides "
"live in :doc:`../how-to/configure-paths`. It is not available on Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:50
msgid ""
"For a ``.py`` script carrying :pep:`723` metadata, pipx builds a temporary "
"wheel from the script and its declared dependencies, installs that wheel "
"like any other package, then records the original path or URL so ``upgrade`` "
"and ``reinstall`` can rebuild it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:78
msgid "Running an application"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:80
msgid ""
"``pipx run APP`` executes an application without installing it permanently. "
"Under the pip backend pipx either reuses a cached temporary venv or builds a "
"fresh one, then invokes the app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:83
msgid ""
"The cache key is a hash of the requirements (the spec plus any ``--with`` "
"packages, with local paths made absolute), the ``--python`` value, pip and "
"venv arguments, the backend, the cooldown, and the installer's environment "
"variables (``PIP_*``, or ``UV_*`` under the uv backend, in any case and with "
"``-`` or ``_``, as ``pip`` reads them). pipx leaves out a short list of "
"variables that cannot change what gets installed, such as timeouts, retries, "
"verbosity, progress bars, color and cache directories, so they do not fork "
"the cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:89
msgid ""
"The key also covers the variables outside those prefixes that ``pip`` or "
"``uv`` read, in any case:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:91
msgid ""
"config files: ``XDG_CONFIG_HOME``, ``XDG_CONFIG_DIRS``, ``APPDATA``, "
"``SYSTEMDRIVE``, ``WIN_PD_OVERRIDE_APPDATA`` and "
"``WIN_PD_OVERRIDE_COMMON_APPDATA``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:93
msgid ""
"TLS trust: ``SSL_CERT_FILE``, ``SSL_CERT_DIR``, ``SSL_CLIENT_CERT``, "
"``REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE`` and ``CURL_CA_BUNDLE``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:94
msgid ""
"proxies: ``HTTP_PROXY``, ``HTTPS_PROXY``, ``ALL_PROXY`` and ``NO_PROXY``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:95
msgid ""
"credentials: ``NETRC``, ``PYTHON_KEYRING_BACKEND``, ``HF_TOKEN``, "
"``PYX_API_KEY``, ``PYX_AUTH_TOKEN`` and the ``AWS_*`` variables ``uv`` reads "
"to sign S3 requests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:98
msgid ""
"``HOME`` and ``USERPROFILE`` stay out: another home means another user, "
"whose default pipx home, and so its cache, already differs. The values only "
"feed the hash, so tokens and proxy passwords never appear in a cache path or "
"a log line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:102
msgid ""
"The hash is an HMAC keyed with a random secret that pipx creates on the "
"first run and keeps in ``.run-key`` inside the cache directory. Other "
"accounts can often list that directory, and without the secret they could "
"hash guesses at a token until one matched an entry's name. On POSIX pipx "
"creates the file with mode ``0600`` and replaces one that another account "
"owns or can read. On Windows it relies on the ACLs of the user profile. When "
"pipx can neither read nor write the secret, as in a read-only cache, it "
"falls back to a plain SHA-256 hash and logs this at debug level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:108
msgid ""
"Cached environments expire after 14 days, after which the next run rebuilds "
"against the latest release. The key leaves out edits to ``pip.conf`` or "
"``uv.toml``, so pass ``--refresh`` after changing them. The temporary venv "
"borrows the shared ``pip``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:112
msgid ""
"Under the uv backend pipx usually hands the whole run to ``uv tool run``, "
"which uses ``uv``'s own cache. ``pipx run --with PKG`` adds extra "
"dependencies to the temporary environment either way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:139
msgid "Exposing apps on PATH"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:141
msgid ""
"When you type an exposed command, the shell finds the symlink (or copy) in "
"``PIPX_BIN_DIR`` and follows it to the launcher inside the app's venv. That "
"launcher runs the venv's own Python against the installed package, so the "
"app always uses its isolated dependencies and never your system site-"
"packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:161
msgid "Directory layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:163
msgid ""
"pipx keeps its venvs and shared libraries under one home directory; the run "
"cache and logs use the platform cache and log directories unless "
"``PIPX_HOME`` is set. The tree below is the conceptual shape; the concrete "
"locations, defaults, and every override live in :doc:`../how-to/configure-"
"paths`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:191
msgid ""
"You can do all of this yourself; pipx automates it. Pass ``--verbose`` to "
"see each command it runs and to stream installer output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:196
msgid "Resolving the Python interpreter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:198
msgid ""
"pipx prefers a real system Python and only downloads a standalone build as a "
"fallback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:200
msgid ""
"When you pass ``--python``, it tries the value as a literal path, then as a "
"command on ``PATH``, then as a ``pythonX.Y`` command, then through the "
"``py`` launcher when one is on ``PATH``. Outside Windows pipx asks the "
"launcher only for an ``X`` or ``X.Y`` version, the one form the Python "
"Launcher for Unix reads as a version request. Only if every step fails, and "
"``--fetch-python=missing`` is set, does pipx fetch a build from `python-"
"build-standalone <https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone>`_. "
"``--fetch-python=always`` skips these steps and downloads a build. The "
"default, ``--fetch-python=never``, keeps pipx offline and errors out instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-pipx-works.rst:209
msgid ""
"For the full step-by-step order, the ``--fetch-python`` values, and when a "
"downloaded build beats a patched system Python, see :doc:`../how-to/"
"standalone-python`."
msgstr ""
